# NAMESPACE=ledger-production

# =============================================================================
# GOA.DESIGN SPECIFIC NOTES
# =============================================================================
#
# Goa Framework Considerations:
#
# 1. OpenAPI Documentation:
#    - Set GOA_OPENAPI_ENABLED=true to serve Swagger UI
#    - Customize paths and metadata for your API
#    - Use different paths for different environments
#
# 2. CORS Configuration:
#    - Essential for web applications consuming your API
#    - Be restrictive with origins in production
#    - Allow credentials only when necessary
#
# 3. Security:
#    - JWT is the most common auth method for Goa APIs
#    - Use RS256 in production with proper key management
#    - API key auth is useful for service-to-service communication
#
# 4. Middleware:
#    - Request ID helps with request tracing
#    - Metrics integration works well with Prometheus
#    - Health checks are essential for container orchestration
#
# 5. Rate Limiting:
#    - Protect your API from abuse
#    - Adjust limits based on your capacity
#    - Consider per-user vs per-IP limiting
#
# 6. File Uploads:
#    - Set appropriate size limits
#    - Validate file types strictly
#    - Consider using cloud storage for large files
#
# 7. Circuit Breaker:
#    - Useful for external service calls
#    - Prevents cascade failures
#    - Monitor failure patterns
#
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# USAGE EXAMPLES
# =============================================================================
#
# Load environment variables in different ways:
#
# 1. Source the file:
#    source .env
#
# 2. Use with Docker:
#    docker run --env-file .env your-app
#
# 3. Use with Docker Compose:
#    Add to docker-compose.yml:
#    services:
#      app:
#        env_file: .env
#
# 4. Use with systemd service:
#    Add to service file:
#    EnvironmentFile=/path/to/.env
#
